maya (Docs): Quick thread  I'm opening a small docs PR to modernize the starter quickstart: switch cURL -> fetch, clarify ephemeral auth flows, and add a minimal "first deploy" checklist. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/12999

ton y (Eng): Heads-up: runtime renamed the streaming endpoints; use /v1/responses/stream for SSE. Also param rename: max_output_tokens -> max_tokens.

kevin (DevEx): For the fetch examples, do we show both browser fetch and node-fetch (for the auth-proxy example)? I can add a tiny proxy plus note about not committing tokens.

maya (Docs): Yes please both. Keep the proxy one-file and show env var REDWOOD_EPHEMERAL_TOKEN. Small deploy checklist: bump Node to 20, include KMS step for Private, and note WebSocket host pattern for Dedicated.

ton y (Eng): Also update SDK snippets: client.responses.create -> client.responses.generate in TS. That will trip up users copying old code.

ops-bot: preview available: https://deploy-preview-12999--docs.redwood.ai.netlify.app :rocket:

kevin (DevEx): sample proxy snippet to include in README:

```js
// auth-proxy.js (local dev)
const http = require('http');
const fetch = require('node-fetch');
http.createServer(async (req, res) => {
  const body = await new Promise(r => { let d=''; req.on('data',c=>d+=c); req.on('end',()=>r(d)); });
  const up = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/responses', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type':'application/json', 'Authorization': `Bearer ${process.env.REDWOOD_EPHEMERAL_TOKEN}` },
    body
  });
  res.writeHead(up.status, { 'content-type': 'application/json' });
  res.end(await up.text());
}).listen(3000);
```

maya (Docs): Nice. I've replaced the cURL blocks with fetch and the node proxy, fixed the link to Dedicated setup, and added the Node 20 Docker base. Waiting on Tony for runtime sanity check.

ton y (Eng): Ran snippet tests locally against staging runtime. Verified fetch + proxy + SDK generate call. All good. Merge when CI is green.

